 "performances": [
  {"date": "2023-07-11", "venue": "Orion Amphitheater", "city": "Huntsville", "state": "AL", "gap": 1962, "set": "2", "note": "Phish debut.", "prev": "Lonely Trip", "next": "Chalk Dust Torture", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-19", "venue": "Live Oak Bank Pavilion at Riverfront Park", "city": "Wilmington", "state": "NC", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "> from \"Chalk Dust Torture.\" The second version of \"Oblivion\" gets taken for a big-time walk. This is grimy, dirty Phish; no bliss jamming or peaks to be found. Page on the synth, heavy effects from Trey, this is a truly exploratory jam.", "prev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "in": ">", "next": "The Wedge", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-23", "venue": "St. Joseph's Health Amphitheater at Lakeview", "city": "Syracuse", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The second leg of a mammoth 1-2 punch following \"Tweezer\", \"Oblivion\" proves to be a prime vehicle for synth-drenched improvisation. A late-night, portentous atmosphere persists until the pivot to major shortly after 11:00, bringing to bear an encouraging blissful payoff.", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": "->", "next": "Miss You", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-29", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Fuego", "in": ">", "next": "Wingsuit", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-08-31", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Beneath a Sea of Stars Part 1", "next": "Light", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-10-06", "venue": "Bridgestone Arena", "city": "Nashville", "state": "TN", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "- > from a \"Jibboo\" worth your time. This sprawling jam starts patiently as the band jams around the structure of the song for a good bit before spreading its wings. Ever so slowly, the tempo gradually builds until things reach a \"mini-peak\" before Trey winds things back to sing the chorus again.", "prev": "Gotta Jibboo", "in": "->", "next": "Torn and Frayed", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-10-14", "venue": "United Center", "city": "Chicago", "state": "IL", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "in": "->", "next": "Split Open and Melt", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-12-29", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a brief stay in the minor synth zone, the jam trends more upbeat by 8:00 and shortly thereafter features more seriously rocking riffage, then deftly turns on the hose with a few long sustained notes from Trey along the way for a surefire crowd-pleasing conclusion.", "prev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "in": ">", "next": "What's the Use?", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-02-22", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "A Wave of Hope", "in": ">", "next": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-04-21", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Down with Disease", "xprev": "Character Zero", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-07-20", "venue": "Xfinity Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 1, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "You Enjoy Myself", "in": ">", "next": "No Men In No Man's Land", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-07-28", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Dirt", "next": "Light", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-07", "venue": "Van Andel Arena", "city": "Grand Rapids", "state": "MI", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Big first set version brings the heat and stays punchy and rocking throughout. Capped off by some fine trilling and a relatively satisfying peak before returning to the lyrics to finish", "prev": "Undermind", "in": ">", "next": "Driver", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-17", "venue": "The Woodlands", "city": "Dover", "state": "DE", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "prev": "Also Sprach Zarathustra", "in": ">", "next": "Down with Disease", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-31", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "While the band may not cover a lot of new ground, they certainly traverse a lot of interesting territory. The song's signature line (which many have already likened to \"Sand\") runs, at least for some time, \"like\" Sand. Moody, atmospheric play does break for airier sounds, with Trey splashing through sonic soil, the version becoming an airier affair. Page pounces, and the second \"half\" of the jam is marked by great full-band play before a return to song, proper, to close.", "prev": "46 Days", "next": "Axilla (Part II)", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-12-28", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Reba", "next": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-01-31", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Something 'haunting' about \"Oblivion's\" opening when done right, and that's the case here. Always moody (one way or the other), the tune is a choice second set opener, and Trey opts for immediate excellence after crashing through the song proper, with the band finding a proper groove right around 5:30. Trey and Page pair from the jump, with the improv, some of the very best kind, finding Trey seemingly playing with two minds, somehow splashing different, concentric ideas - in a manner of thinking - off the other, in a manner (or sound) similar to one of his heroes.", "next": "Sightless Escape", "xprev": "Possum", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-04-26", "venue": "Hollywood Bowl", "city": "Hollywood", "state": "CA", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "The Howling", "in": ">", "next": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-06-22", "venue": "SNHU Arena", "city": "Manchester", "state": "NH", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "prev": "Runaway Jim", "next": "The Curtain With", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-04", "venue": "Folsom Field", "city": "Boulder", "state": "CO", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "A typically jaunty, groovy improvisation makes a break for more pastoral, psychedelic territories around the 6:30 mark. With Fishman's pocket remaining constant and ever rock-solid, Trey, Page and Mike's particularly funky affected tones help to create an intoxicatingly textural dance party, before the \"Oblivion\" closing section emerges to close it out.", "prev": "Rift", "next": "Timber (Jerry the Mule)", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-18", "venue": "United Center", "city": "Chicago", "state": "IL", "gap": 7, "set": "1", "prev": "Harry Hood", "next": "Heavy Things", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-26", "venue": "Broadview Stage at SPAC", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Down with Disease", "xprev": "No Men In No Man's Land", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-09-16", "venue": "Ameris Bank Amphitheatre", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Breaks apart early on via a major mode shift, as a spacey loop from Trey creates an airy vibe on top of Fishman's strong foundation. The music shifts back to minor, with Mike's melodic basslines and Page's enveloping synths curating an introspective atmosphere. Optimism then begins to peek out of the haze, as Trey begins to tear off some delightfully spry leads, eventually driving this psychedelic affair towards a celebratory crescendo to close it all out.", "next": "David Bowie", "xprev": "The Squirming Coil", "nb": 1},
